# Gruum design tokens

`tokens.css` is the source of truth, copied from the Gruum-UI-Design Figma file. Use these custom properties and classes for all new UI. Do not introduce new colors, type scales, radii, or shadows unless they are added to `tokens.css` from Figma.

## Colors

`var(--background)` `--white` `--dark` `--primary-base` `--primary-light` `--error-base` `--error-light` `--error-faded` `--text-primary` `--text-secondary` `--text-tertiary` `--text-light` `--fade-dark-10` `--fade-dark-15` `--fade-dark-20` `--fade-white-60` `--green-base` `--green-faded` `--variant-base` `--variant-faded` `--semantic-button`

## Numbers

`var(--xsmall)` `2px`, `--number` `6px`, `--corner-small` `8px`, `--corner-medium` `10px`, `--corner-full` `999px`

## Text

Classes: `.headline-main` `.headline-secondary` `.headline-small` `.body-large-bold` `.body-normal` `.body-normal-bold` `.body-small` `.body-small-bold` `.body-xsmall` `.token-regular` `.token-bold`

Headlines use PP Neue Montreal (fallback Inter). Body uses Inter. Token/code uses DM Mono.

## Effects

`var(--shadow-card-hard)` `--shadow-card-soft` `--shadow-button-primary` `--shadow-button-white` `--shadow-button-secondary` `--shadow-modal-base`

## Stack

Static Vite MPA, HTML/CSS/JS. Do not add Tailwind unless asked.
